# Project context

- Read PROJECT_SPEC.md before doing anything. It is the source of truth.
- This project uses Supabase as the backend. It does NOT use Django.
- This is an unofficial study tool. Never use Microsoft logos or trademarked artwork. Keep the "Unofficial" label visible.

# Locked files

- Never edit src/features/quiz/types.ts or src/features/quiz/data/questions.ts. If a change seems needed, stop and ask.

# Locked structure

- Follow the folder structure in PROJECT_SPEC.md exactly. Do not invent new top-level folders or move files without asking.

# TypeScript

- Strict mode. Never write `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow it.
- Interfaces for object shapes, union types instead of enums, typed props without React.FC.

# Security

- The Claude API key must only exist in Supabase function secrets. Never put it in client code, .env files that are committed, or the repo.
- Never log or expose secrets.

# Working style

- Plan first and show the plan. Then build one chunk at a time (see PROJECT_SPEC.md section 8).
- After each chunk, summarize what changed and why, then stop and wait for review.
- Do not add dependencies without saying why.
- Do not change the visual tokens in PROJECT_SPEC.md section 6.
- Commits: Conventional Commits type prefix on the summary line, then a body with one bullet per logical change.
